# CMake build output. `build-*` as well as `build/`: run-checks.sh puts each
# sanitizer and the clang lane in its own tree beside it, and without the glob
# they were committed -- 534 object files carrying one machine's absolute paths,
# which then made every sanitizer lane fail to configure anywhere else.
build/
build-*/
_CPack_Packages/

# Packaged artifacts
*.deb

# Agent worktrees. `session-compare.sh` and the parity work both build a
# baseline in a git worktree under here; a worktree's `.git` file makes it look
# like an embedded repository, and `git add -A` will happily track it as a
# gitlink pointing at a path that exists on one machine.
.claude/worktrees/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
